  "result": "`satisfies(version, range)` is now implemented in `src/semver.js` following `docs/SPEC.md`. `npm test` passes, 11 tests with 0 failures.\n\nThe new tests are in `test/satisfies.test.js`. They cover version parsing and invalid input, prerelease ordering, comparators, x-ranges and partials, tilde, caret, hyphen ranges and the prerelease rule. Every case comes from the spec's tables and examples or an edge case I derived from the spec text.\n\nThe spec doesn't say what to do in these cases, so I chose:\n- **`>*` and `<*`:** these match nothing, while `>=*` and `<=*` match anything.\n- **Spaces after `~` or `^`:** `~ 1.2.3` is treated as an invalid range and returns `false`, because the spec only allows whitespace after comparator operators.\n- **Leading zeros in numeric prerelease identifiers:** `1.0.0-01` is accepted, because the spec only forbids leading zeros in MAJOR, MINOR and PATCH.\n- **Hyphen ranges:** `A - B` is recognised when it sits inside a set with other comparators, and each side must be a plain version with no operator.",
